      "id": "isthmus_7702_extcodesize_extcodehash",
      "comment": "Two txs in one block: tx0 installs a 7702 delegation on AUTH (addr5) pointing at MARKER (reusing the B1 pattern, but this vector's `to` is a no-op call target -- the deadbeef predeploy stand-in address 0x...dEaD -- so nothing else runs in tx0 besides authorization processing); tx1 is a plain EIP-1559 call into a PROBER contract that does EXTCODESIZE(AUTH)->slot0 and EXTCODEHASH(AUTH)->slot1. Per EIP-7702, both opcodes must observe the 23-byte delegation indicator (0xef0100||target), NOT MARKER's own (6-byte) code or codehash -- a classic 7702 gotcha (external observers see the indicator, only internal calls actually execute the delegate's code).",
